text: ['({B/G} can be paid with either {B} or {G}.)\\nTrample\\nAt the beginning of your end step, return to your hand all creature cards in your graveyard that were put there from the battlefield this turn.', '({T}: Add {B}.)', '({T}: Add {G}.)', '({T}: Add {R}.)', '({T}: Add {U}.)', '({U/R} can be paid with either {U} or {R}.)\\nFlying\\nEach instant and sorcery spell you cast has replicate. The replicate cost is equal to its mana cost. (When you cast it, copy it for each time you paid its replicate cost. You may choose new targets for the copies.)', '({U/R} can be paid with either {U} or {R}.)\\n{2}{U}: Copy target instant spell you control with mana value 2 or less. You may choose new targets for the copy.\\n{2}{R}: Copy target sorcery spell you control with mana value 2 or less. You may choose new targets for the copy.', "All lands you control become 1/1 creatures until end of turn. They're still lands.", "At the beginning of your upkeep, you may look at the top card of your library. You may cast it without paying its mana cost if it's an instant or sorcery spell.", 'Barren Moor enters the battlefield tapped.\\n{T}: Add {B}.\\nCycling {B} ({B}, Discard this card: Draw a card.)', "Boneyard Wurm's power and toughness are each equal to the number of creature cards in your graveyard.", 'Choose one —\\n• Counter target noncreature spell unless its controller pays {2}.\\n• Izzet Charm deals 2 damage to target creature.\\n• Draw two cards, then discard two cards.', "Choose one —\\n• Create a 2/2 black Zombie creature token.\\n• Destroy target nonartifact, nonblack creature. It can't be regenerated.", 'Choose one —\\n• Draw X cards.\\n• Invoke the Firemind deals X damage to any target.', "Counter target creature spell. Draw cards equal to that spell's mana value.", 'Counter target spell unless its controller pays {1}.', "Counter target spell. If that spell is countered this way, exile it instead of putting it into its owner's graveyard.", 'Dakmor Salvage enters the battlefield tapped.\\n{T}: Add {B}.\\nDredge 2 (If you would draw a card, you may mill two cards instead. If you do, return this card from your graveyard to your hand.)', "Destroy target artifact or creature. It can't be regenerated.", 'Draw a card for each creature card in your graveyard.', 'Draw three cards, then put two cards from your hand on top of your library in any order.', 'Dredge 3 (If you would draw a card, you may mill three cards instead. If you do, return this card from your graveyard to your hand.)', 'Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature has "{T}: This creature deals 1 damage to target player or planeswalker. You draw a card."', 'Enchant creature\\nWhen a creature dies, destroy enchanted creature.', 'Fire deals 2 damage divided as you choose among one or two targets.', 'Flying\\nWhenever Stinkweed Imp deals combat damage to a creature, destroy that creature.\\nDredge 5 (If you would draw a card, you may mill five cards instead. If you do, return this card from your graveyard to your hand.)', 'Flying\\nWhenever you cast an instant or sorcery spell, Wee Dragonauts gets +2/+0 until end of turn.', 'Flying\\nWhenever you draw a card, Niv-Mizzet, the Firemind deals 1 damage to any target.\\n{T}: Draw a card.', 'Forgotten Cave enters the battlefield tapped.\\n{T}: Add {R}.\\nCycling {R} ({R}, Discard this card: Draw a card.)', 'Golgari Grave-Troll enters the battlefield with a +1/+1 counter on it for each creature card in your graveyard.\\n{1}, Remove a +1/+1 counter from Golgari Grave-Troll: Regenerate Golgari Grave-Troll.\\nDredge 6 (If you would draw a card, you may mill six cards instead. If you do, return this card from your graveyard to your hand.)', "Golgari Rot Farm enters the battlefield tapped.\\nWhen Golgari Rot Farm enters the battlefield, return a land you control to its owner's hand.\\n{T}: Add {B}{G}.", "Haste\\nScavenge {3}{B}{G} ({3}{B}{G}, Exile this card from your graveyard: Put a number of +1/+1 counters equal to this card's power on target creature. Scavenge only as a sorcery.)", 'Imprint — When Isochron Scepter enters the battlefield, you may exile an instant card with mana value 2 or less from your hand.\\n{2}, {T}: You may copy the exiled card. If you do, you may cast the copy without paying its mana cost.', 'Instant and sorcery spells you cast cost {1} less to cast.', "Intimidate (This creature can't be blocked except by artifact creatures and/or creatures that share a color with it.)\\nSacrifice Brain Weevil: Target player discards two cards. Activate only as a sorcery.", "Izzet Boilerworks enters the battlefield tapped.\\nWhen Izzet Boilerworks enters the battlefield, return a land you control to its owner's hand.\\n{T}: Add {U}{R}.", "Jarad, Golgari Lich Lord gets +1/+1 for each creature card in your graveyard.\\n{1}{B}{G}, Sacrifice another creature: Each opponent loses life equal to the sacrificed creature's power.\\nSacrifice a Swamp and a Forest: Return Jarad from your graveyard to your hand.", 'Lonely Sandbar enters the battlefield tapped.\\n{T}: Add {U}.\\nCycling {U} ({U}, Discard this card: Draw a card.)', 'Magma Spray deals 2 damage to target creature. If that creature would die this turn, exile it instead.', 'Pay 2 life: Putrid Leech gets +2/+2 until end of turn. Activate only once each turn.', 'Prophetic Bolt deals 4 damage to any target. Look at the top four cards of your library. Put one of those cards into your hand and the rest on the bottom of your library in any order.', 'Reach\\nWhen Stingerfling Spider enters the battlefield, you may destroy target creature with flying.', 'Replicate {1}{R} (When you cast this spell, copy it for each time you paid its replicate cost. You may choose new targets for the copies.)\\nPyromatics deals 1 damage to any target.', 'Replicate {1}{U} (When you cast this spell, copy it for each time you paid its replicate cost.)\\nDraw a card.', "Replicate {2}{U} (When you cast this spell, copy it for each time you paid its replicate cost. You may choose new targets for the copies.)\\nReturn target creature to its owner's hand.", 'Replicate {2}{U} (When you cast this spell, copy it for each time you paid its replicate cost.)\\nCreate a 3/3 blue Weird creature token with defender and flying. Exile it at the beginning of the next end step.', 'Return target creature card from your graveyard to the battlefield. If {G} was spent to cast this spell, that creature enters the battlefield with an additional +1/+1 counter on it.', "Return target creature to its owner's hand. Its controller draws a card.", 'Return up to three target land cards from your graveyard to your hand.\\nDredge 3 (If you would draw a card, you may mill three cards instead. If you do, return this card from your graveyard to your hand.)', 'Sacrifice Shambling Shell: Put a +1/+1 counter on target creature.\\nDredge 3 (If you would draw a card, you may mill three cards instead. If you do, return this card from your graveyard to your hand.)', 'Sacrifice a creature: Target player discards two cards. Activate only as a sorcery.', "Shrewd Hatchling enters the battlefield with four -1/-1 counters on it.\\n{U/R}: Target creature can't block Shrewd Hatchling this turn.\\nWhenever you cast a blue spell, remove a -1/-1 counter from Shrewd Hatchling.\\nWhenever you cast a red spell, remove a -1/-1 counter from Shrewd Hatchling.", 'Street Spasm deals X damage to target creature without flying you don\'t control.\\nOverload {X}{X}{R}{R} (You may cast this spell for its overload cost. If you do, change "target" in its text to "each.")', 'Target creature gets +X/+0 until end of turn, where X is the number of creature cards in your graveyard.', 'Target player reveals their hand. You choose a card from it. That player discards that card.\\nDredge 2 (If you would draw a card, you may mill two cards instead. If you do, return this card from your graveyard to your hand.)', 'Target player shuffles their graveyard into their library.', "Trample\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, sacrifice a creature. You gain life equal to that creature's toughness.", 'Tranquil Thicket enters the battlefield tapped.\\n{T}: Add {G}.\\nCycling {G} ({G}, Discard this card: Draw a card.)', 'When Eternal Witness enters the battlefield, you may return target card from your graveyard to your hand.', 'When Golgari Thug dies, put target creature card from your graveyard on top of your library.\\nDredge 4 (If you would draw a card, you may mill four cards instead. If you do, return this card from your graveyard to your hand.)', 'When Izzet Chronarch enters the battlefield, return target instant or sorcery card from your graveyard to your hand.', "When Ogre Savant enters the battlefield, if {U} was spent to cast it, return target creature to its owner's hand.", 'When Ravenous Rats enters the battlefield, target opponent discards a card.', 'When Steamcore Weird enters the battlefield, if {R} was spent to cast it, it deals 2 damage to any target.', 'Whenever a nontoken creature you control dies, create a 1/1 green Saproling creature token.', 'Whenever you cast an instant or sorcery spell, Kiln Fiend gets +3/+0 until end of turn.', 'Whenever you cast an instant or sorcery spell, you may put a charge counter on Sphinx-Bone Wand. If you do, Sphinx-Bone Wand deals damage equal to the number of charge counters on it to any target.', "You may cast Twilight's Call as though it had flash if you pay {2} more to cast it. (You may cast it any time you could cast an instant.)\\nEach player returns all creature cards from their graveyard to the battlefield.", '{1}, {T}: Add {B}{G}.', '{1}, {T}: Add {U}{R}.', '{1}{B}: Return Reassembling Skeleton from your graveyard to the battlefield tapped.', "{1}{B}{G}: Target creature gets +1/+1 and gains intimidate until end of turn. (It can't be blocked except by artifact creatures and/or creatures that share a color with it.)\\n{2}{B}{G}, Sacrifice a nontoken creature: Create X 1/1 green Saproling creature tokens, where X is the sacrificed creature's toughness.", '{B}, Sacrifice a creature: Target creature gets -1/-1 until end of turn.', '{B}, Sacrifice a creature: Target player loses 1 life.', '{T}: Add {B}. Elves of Deep Shadow deals 1 damage to you.', "{T}: Add {C}.\\n{2}{U}{R}, {T}: Exile the top card of your library. Until your next turn, you may cast it if it's an instant or sorcery spell.", '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{3}{B}{G}: Until end of turn, Svogthos, the Restless Tomb becomes a black and green Plant Zombie creature with "This creature\'s power and toughness are each equal to the number of creature cards in your graveyard." It\'s still a land.', '{T}: Gelectrode deals 1 damage to any target.\\nWhenever you cast an instant or sorcery spell, you may untap Gelectrode.']
flavor: ['"All matter, animate or not, rots when exposed to time. We merely speed up the process."\\n—Ezoc, Golgari rot farmer', '"But then . . . oh, but . . . which means . . . which would lead to . . . exactly!"', '"Diametrically opposing energies in self-sealed plasmodermic bubbles make great pets!"\\n—Trivaz, Izzet mage', '"I don\'t *think* so."', '"Jund is a wounded world. Beware its searing blood spilling out onto the surface."\\n—Rakka Mar', '"Look at her, once filled with innocence. Death has a way of wringing away such . . . deficiencies."\\n—Savra', '"My brain hurts."', '"Nothing in nature goes to waste, not even the rotting corpse of a good-for-nothing, blood-sucking vampire."\\n—Halana of Ulvenwald', '"The blazekite is a simple concept, really—just a vehicular application of dragscoop ionics and electropropulsion magnetronics."\\n—Juzba, Izzet tinker', '"The living cannot understand the benefits of death."\\n—Chaeska, Keeper of Tresserhorn', '"They may show up with the wrong thigh bone or mandible, but they always show up."\\n—Zul Ashur, lich lord', '"This abomination never belonged in our world. I\'m merely setting it free."\\n—Dierk, geistmage', '"Victory in the pits is almost as rewarding as the methods I use to achieve it."', 'After fear and weakness rot away, that which remains is stronger than its living form.', 'Cast out of the Conclave generations ago, these elves found a home in the corrupted districts of the Golgari.', 'Depending on your point of view, the seal represents a proud guardian of the natural cycle or one who has sold her soul to darkness for eternal life.', "Devouring books is only the beginning. The librarian's next.", 'He ensures not only whether but also when and where the lightning strikes twice.', "He's an oxymoron.", "It chews open Mirrodin's husk and feeds on the outpouring of energy.", 'It eats and eats until the juiciest morsel it can find is itself.', "It reacted to Naya's overabundant food supply by growing additional mouths.", 'It traps an explosion within its stony skin.', "Its host's final curse lies captured within.", 'Leave the door to the past even slightly ajar and it could be blown off its hinges.', 'Like corpse-worms through a carapace, rotwurms slide through the hollowed bones of the undercity.', 'Like many Izzet creations, weirds are based on wild contradictions yet somehow manage to work.', "Man's best fungus.", 'Mercadians not wealthy enough to buy a tomb are thrown into a bog called "the Ghoul\'s Larder."', "Niv-Mizzet's genius and vanity reverberate throughout the mirrored halls of Nivix.", 'On Bant, a sigil is both a prize of honor and a bond of duty. The one who bears it may be called to fulfill that charge at any moment.', "She remembers every word spoken, from the hero's oath to the baby's cry.", "The Golgari don't bury their dead. They plant them.", 'The Izzet signet is redesigned often, each time becoming closer to a vanity portrait of Niv-Mizzet.', 'The clouds grew thick, and then they grew teeth.', "The demon's yoke is part leash, part noose.", 'The dwarves call their quicksilver techniques "improvisational weaponsmithing."', 'The juiciest prey is that which grows lazy, thinking itself beyond the reach of danger.', 'The mizzium-sphere array drove her mind deep into the thought field, where only the rarest motes of genius may be plucked.', 'The only thing it likes more than discovering a pit of bones is adding to it.', 'To those in tune with the Firemind, there is no difference between knowledge and flame.', 'Twilight falls. We rise.\\n—Necropolis inscription', 'When asked how much power is required, Izzet mages always answer "more."']
